# Canister Tycoon — Cyberpunk Server & Node Survival Simulator
### Game Design Document (GDD) & Technical Architecture Guide

---

## 1. Executive Summary & Game Pitch

* **Title:** Canister Tycoon: Subnet Zero
* **Genre:** Automation / Base-Builder / Strategy Tycoon (*Factorio* meets *Cyberpunk 2077* & *Silicon Valley*)
* **Platform:** Next.js (Web / Desktop / Mobile Web)
* **On-Chain Backend:** Internet Computer via `@icp-sdk/core` / `icp-coresdk` canisters
* **Visual Style:** 2D Isometric Cyberpunk Pixel Art with glowing neon bloom shaders, animated data-packet streams, and dynamic heat-map overlays.
* **Core Hook:** You are an underground rogue node operator in a dystopian, heavily monitored digital future. You design, wire, cool, and protect modular server racks, fiber-optic bandwidth pipelines, and decentralized compute canisters against thermal overloads, botnet DDoS raids, and corporate power blackouts.

---

## 2. Core Pillars & Player Fantasy

1. **Intricate Engineering & Layout Optimization:** Every rack, wire, and pipe matters. Poor cable management creates thermal bottlenecks; unshielded power supplies blow fuses.
2. **High-Stakes Live Operations:** Real-time events force tactical choices — do you overclock your GPUs to capture a high-yield transaction spike, risking a catastrophic fire?
3. **True Sovereign Ownership:** Save games, node blueprints, hardware perks, and global leaderboard rankings are verified and stored directly in your personal on-chain canister using `icp-coresdk`.

