## 4. Hardware & Infrastructure Catalog

### 4.1. Compute & Storage Nodes
| Tier | Hardware Unit | Compute Power (MIPS) | Heat Output | Power Draw | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Tier 1** | *Refurbished Blade 2040* | 50 MIPS | +15°C | 120W | Cheap starting unit. Prone to hardware jitter. |
| **Tier 2** | *Silicon-Core Canister Array* | 250 MIPS | +45°C | 400W | Balanced workhorse for stable canister hosting. |
| **Tier 3** | *Neural Matrix Accelerator (AI)* | 1,200 MIPS | +110°C | 1,100W | Massive yield on AI smart contracts, extreme heat. |
| **Tier 4** | *Quantum Gate Q-8* | 5,000 MIPS | +250°C | 2,800W | Requires cryo-liquid cooling. Zero latency throughput. |

### 4.2. Cooling & Thermal Management
* **Passive Heat Sinks:** Cheap, 0W power, but only dissipates minor ambient heat.
* **High-RPM Fan Arrays:** Low cost, noisy, requires exhaust duct placement.
* **Closed-Loop Liquid Tubes:** Routes coolant from server racks to radiator blocks.
* **Liquid Nitrogen Cryo-Pods:** Heavy power cost, cools adjacent 3x3 tiles to -10°C.
* **Sub-Immersion Mineral Oil Tanks:** Eliminates fire risk, high upfront capital investment.

### 4.3. Power & Energy Infrastructure
* **Grid Tap (Street Line):** Cheap baseline power, but vulnerable to city brownouts and utility tariff spikes.
* **Diesel Generator Sub-Station:** Backup power during outages; requires buying fuel barrels.
* **Solar Rooftop Arrays:** Free daytime energy, zero power during cyber-storms.
* **Nuclear Micro-Reactor (Late Game):** Massive clean energy, requires radiation shielding.

### 4.4. Networking & Security
* **Cat-8 Copper Lines:** Basic short-range bandwidth routing.
* **Fiber-Optic Laser Trunk:** High throughput, ultra-low latency.
* **Hardware Firewall Gateway:** Automatically filters 80% of low-grade botnet packets.
* **Honeypot Decoy Rack:** Diverts hacker attacks away from your primary database canisters.

