## 5. Thermodynamics & Resource Economy

### 5.1. Resource Formulas

1. **Cycle Earnings per Second ($E$):**
   $$E = (\text{Total Compute MIPS} \times \text{Network Quality}) \times \text{Multiplier}_{\text{overclock}} - \text{Latency Penalty}$$

2. **Thermal Dissipation Balance:**
   $$\Delta T = \sum \text{Heat}_{\text{Hardware}} - \sum \text{Cooling}_{\text{Active}} - \text{Ambient Dissipation}$$
   * If Rack Temp > 85°C: **Thermal Throttling (-50% Output)**
   * If Rack Temp > 105°C: **Hardware Melt & Catastrophic Fire**

3. **Power Grid Stability:**
   $$\text{Load Ratio} = \frac{\text{Power Required}}{\text{Power Supply Capacity}}$$
   * If $\text{Load Ratio} > 1.0$: Circuit breaker trips; whole cluster powers down.

